[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="ElementChartResource" load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/combat/resources/ElementChartResource.gd" id="1_elchart"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_elchart")
elements = Array[StringName]([&"fire", &"water", &"nature", &"wind", &"earth", &"holy", &"dark"])
default_multiplier = 1.0
matrix = {
&"dark": {
&"dark": 0.75,
&"holy": 1.25
},
&"earth": {
&"earth": 0.75,
&"water": 1.25
},
&"fire": {
&"fire": 0.75,
&"nature": 1.25
},
&"holy": {
&"dark": 1.25,
&"holy": 0.75
},
&"nature": {
&"fire": 1.25,
&"nature": 0.75
},
&"water": {
&"earth": 1.25,
&"water": 0.75
},
&"wind": {
&"wind": 0.75
}
}
notes = "SEEDED MATCHUPS -- the framework's starting numbers. Balancing is content work:
edit the floats here, not the code.

TWO RULES generated every entry below.

1. EVERY ELEMENT RESISTS ITSELF -- 0.75.
   fire>fire, water>water, nature>nature, wind>wind, earth>earth, holy>holy,
   dark>dark. Seven entries. A unit is hardest to hurt with its own element, so
   a mirror match is decided by play rather than by the chart.

2. OPPOSITE PAIRS ARE STRONG BOTH WAYS -- 1.25, authored in both directions.
   fire <-> nature   (flame burns wood; green chokes out flame)
   water <-> earth   (water erodes stone; earth dams water)
   holy <-> dark     (the classic opposition)
   Six entries -- each pair is listed once per direction, never inferred.

   fire<->nature is the pair with live content today (18 nature moves, 6 nature
   characters, 1 fire move) and it is the matchup the existing design already
   leaned on -- Ember Storm into the tree boss. water<->earth is half-live (4
   earth moves, 2 earth characters, no water content yet).

WIND has no opposite. It is the one element with NO content at all -- no move and
no character carries it -- so pairing it now would be inventing balance for
something that does not exist. It self-resists and is otherwise neutral. Give it
an opposite when wind content is authored.

EVERYTHING ELSE IS NEUTRAL (1.0), including every element this file has never
heard of. Unlisted is not an error: a move or character authored with a brand new
element simply plays neutral until someone adds its row here.

TILE ELEMENTS -- `tile_elements` below is THE authority (see its own doc). Every
tile effect that ships today is assigned:

  fire            -> fire     (lava's burn)
  scorching_vent  -> fire     (volcanic vent)
  molten_lava     -> fire     (tile id, for terrain that grows its own effect)
  magma_vent      -> fire     (tile id)
  scorched        -> fire     (the rule flag scorching_vent raises)
  empowering_water-> water    (deep water's aquatic buff)
  slippery_ice    -> water    (frozen surface)
  deep_water      -> water    (tile id)
  tall_grass      -> nature   (concealing grass)
  vine_trap       -> nature   (Petalfang's snare)
  fortify         -> earth    (sacred ground's dug-in defence)
  rock_rubble     -> earth    (broken stone)
  sacred_meadow   -> nature   (see below)

SACRED MEADOW IS NATURE, NOT HOLY -- an authored design call, recorded here because
the name argues the other way. The meadow is a living, growing place that heals,
and its heal is meant to run STRONGER for the nature creatures that belong in it
(the own_tile_effect_bonus path): 10 HP becomes 13 for a nature occupant, and
everyone else -- including a holy one -- gets the authored 10. Elementing it holy
would have handed that affinity to a roster that has no nature relationship with
the ground it is standing on.

DELIBERATELY ELEMENTLESS: `stealth` (a pure rule flag -- it neither damages nor
grants a magnitude, so an element on it would colour a badge and change nothing),
and every tile TYPE that imposes no effect (grass_plains, tree, forest_dirt,
obsidian, snow_field, ...). A tile with nothing to apply has nothing to element:
the badge would promise a matchup the board never resolves."
tile_match_bonus = 1.25
own_tile_benefit = 0.9
own_tile_effect_bonus = 1.25
tile_elements = {
&"deep_water": &"water",
&"empowering_water": &"water",
&"fire": &"fire",
&"fortify": &"earth",
&"magma_vent": &"fire",
&"molten_lava": &"fire",
&"rock_rubble": &"earth",
&"sacred_meadow": &"nature",
&"scorched": &"fire",
&"scorching_vent": &"fire",
&"slippery_ice": &"water",
&"tall_grass": &"nature",
&"vine_trap": &"nature"
}
